            <ArticleTitle>Highly diastereo- and enantioselective synthesis of spirooxindole-cyclohexaneamides through N,N'-dioxide/Ni(ii)-catalyzed Diels-Alder reactions.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2060-2063</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc10125a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Highly efficient asymmetric Diels-Alder reactions of methyleneindolinones with 1,3-dienylcarbamates and 1,2-dihydropyridines have been accomplished by using a chiral N,N'-dioxide/nickel(ii) complex as an efficient catalyst. New kinds of spirooxindole-cyclohexaneamides were achieved in up to 99% yield, &gt;95 : 5 dr, and 99% ee.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
